semantic-plausibility

The initial semantic checking kernel and terminology inventory were extracted
from the Apache-2.0 licensed INTERPOLAR quality_control component at commit
eaf1747a, then adapted into an independent src-layout Python project.
No INTERPOLAR runtime, private data, access credentials or patient extracts
are included. The original license is retained in LICENSE.
Terminology catalogs and implementation guides retain their own licenses.

Runtime profile setup obtains MII ObservationLab from the publisher's pinned
package, attributed to Medizininformatik-Initiative and its authors under
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Source: https://github.com/medizininformatik-initiative/kerndatensatzmodul-labor
Downloaded profiles, ValueSets and CodeSystems remain operator-owned runtime
files and are not distributed in this repository.

The optional local UCUM service installs the official NLM ucum-lhc package
at image-build time. Its upstream licence and notices remain with the installed
dependency: https://github.com/LHNCBC/ucum-lhc

The optional decision service installs the Apache-2.0 Laya runtime:
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
The pinned Apache-2.0 multilingual model is downloaded separately at startup:
https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual
Model files remain in the operator's ignored local/laya cache. Upstream licences
and dependency notices remain with the installed packages and downloaded files.
